 "takeaways": [
  "The whole new mathematics is two short lemmas (2.2 signed matrix A_n has spectrum +-sqrt(n); 2.3 Delta(H) >= lambda_1 of any signed adjacency matrix); everything else on the path to bs(f) <= s(f)^4 is imported: Cauchy interlacing, Gotsman-Linial, Nisan-Szegedy/Tal.",
  "Of 43 statement-level nodes, 24 are external (cited or standard); the main theorem rests on exactly 1 external result (interlacing), the Sensitivity Theorem on 3.",
  "Grounding: interlacing, Courant-Fischer, hypercube graph, principal submatrix, eigenvalue have no hit in the 16K-concept textbook+ProofWiki layer; the proof grounds only to symmetric/square/adjacency matrix, induced subgraph, boolean function.",
  "Rules graph recovers the lemmas but only 1 of 17 result-level dependencies: no edge from Cauchy interlacing (named, no \\ref), Lemma 2.3 downgraded to a mention, and the deg -> s -> bs chain to the Sensitivity Theorem is missing."
 ],
